,"slots":{"content":[{"config":{"icon":"circle-alert","title":{"$i18n":"comments.errors.promoteFailed"},"tone":"danger"},"id":"error","type":"Alert"}]},"type":"Stack"},{"config":{"label":{"$i18n":"reviews.promote.questionLabel"},"placeholder":{"$i18n":"reviews.promote.questionPlaceholder"},"required":true,"valueKey":"comments.sample.message.promoteQuestion"},"id":"question","type":"TextInput"},{"config":{"label":{"$i18n":"reviews.promote.summaryLabel"},"placeholder":{"$i18n":"reviews.promote.summaryPlaceholder"},"required":true},"id":"summary","type":"TextInput"},{"config":{"label":{"$i18n":"reviews.promote.rationaleLabel"},"placeholder":{"$i18n":"reviews.promote.rationalePlaceholder"},"rows":2},"id":"rationale","type":"TextInput"},{"config":{"direction":"horizontal","gap":8,"justify":"end","padding":"4px 0 0"},"id":"footer","slots":{"content":[{"config":{"label":{"$i18n":"common.cancel"},"variant":"ghost"},"id":"cancel","type":"Button"},{"config":{"disabled":true,"label":{"$i18n":"reviews.promote.submit"},"variant":"primary"},"id":"submit","type":"Button"}]},"type":"Stack"}]},"type":"Stack"}]},"type":"Panel"}]},"type":"Stack"},{"config":{"align":"center","direction":"vertical","visible":false,"width":"100%"},"id":"another-wrap","slots":{"content":[{"config":{"backdrop":true,"closable":true,"closeLabel":{"$i18n":"common.close"},"description":{"$i18n":"reviews.promote.anotherDescription"},"maxWidth":"100%","padding":16,"title":{"$i18n":"reviews.promote.anotherTitle"},"variant":"dialog","width":"512px"},"id":"dialog-another","slots":{"content":[{"config":{"direction":"vertical","gap":12},"id":"another-body","slots":{"content":[{"config":{"label":{"$i18n":"reviews.promote.questionLabel"},"placeholder":{"$i18n":"reviews.promote.questionPlaceholder"},"required":true,"valueKey":"comments.sample.message.promoteQuestion"},"id":"another-question","type":"TextInput"},{"config":{"label":{"$i18n":"reviews.promote.summaryLabel"},"placeholder":{"$i18n":"reviews.promote.summaryPlaceholder"},"required":true,"valueKey":"comments.sample.message.promoteOutcome"},"id":"another-summary","type":"TextInput"},{"config":{"label":{"$i18n":"reviews.promote.rationaleLabel"},"placeholder":{"$i18n":"reviews.promote.rationalePlaceholder"},"rows":2},"id":"another-rationale","type":"TextInput"},{"config":{"direction":"horizontal","gap":8,"justify":"end","padding":"4px 0 0"},"id":"another-footer","slots":{"content":[{"config":{"label":{"$i18n":"common.cancel"},"variant":"ghost"},"id":"another-cancel","type":"Button"},{"config":{"label":{"$i18n":"reviews.promote.anotherSubmit"},"variant":"primary"},"id":"another-confirm","type":"Button"}]},"type":"Stack"}]},"type":"Stack"}]},"type":"Panel"}]},"type":"Stack"}]},"type":"Stack"}]},"type":"RootShell"},"name":"Promote to Decision dialog","spec":{"accessibility":["The dialog is named \"Promote to Decision\" and described by its description; required fields are marked as required; the error or conflict is an alert and takes focus, and Esc closes the dialog without promoting."],"constraints":["Built only from Adapter Widgets (Stack, Text, Button, TextInput, Alert, Panel dialog); no Widget outside the Adapter catalog.","The two dialogs (Promote, Create another Decision) are shown one at a time by a Variant, and each alert by its own; the dialog is a Panel with a shadow over the page, not a dimmed Workbench behind a Modal. Required fields carry the asterisk of the Kit field.","The strings of the app are copied under the same Locale keys; the typed question, outcome and rationale are sample strings per Locale, set through their Locale keys by the Variants.","Every visible string is bound with $i18n; en-US and zh-TW keep identical key sets.","Visual language follows the Quiet Canvas design system in DESIGN.md."],"decisions":[],"entryConditions":["A member who may write Decisions chose Promote to Decision, or Create another Decision, from the menu of a thread's bubble or detail, on a desktop or tablet layout; the dialog opens over the page with focus on its first field.","The base state is the dialog opened on an open thread: the question holds the thread's title, the outcome and the rationale are empty and Promote is disabled.","The render context selects one Workspace viewport preset, one Locale and one theme; the dialog is Workbench chrome, so its text follows the Workbench language and is baked here per Locale. The question, the outcome and the rationale are sample content."],"intent":"Show the Promote to Decision dialog of the Workbench as built from Adapter Widgets only: how a discussion on a thread becomes a Decision in the View Spec, with its question, its outcome and the rationale, and how the dialog says that the thread or the View changed under it, or that the promotion failed, while keeping what was typed.","interactionRules":["A thread becomes a Decision only through this explicit step, and only into the View it is anchored to; nothing is promoted automatically, and the dialog's Promote stays disabled until the question and the outcome are filled. The rationale is optional and repeats the outcome when left empty.","Create another Decision is a distinct action, offered once the thread already has a Decision: the same form under its own title says the earlier Decision stays as it is.","A promotion refused for a conflict names what moved, the thread, the View or both, keeps every entry, loads the latest version and asks the member to confirm again; it never sends the promotion by itself. A promotion that failed for another reason shows its error inside the dialog, which takes focus there."],"references":[{"label":"Phase 5 of the closed loop: dogfood coverage of the core surfaces","relation":"decision","type":"external","uri":"https://github.com/DevilTea/uiux/discussions/379#discussioncomment-19257377"},{"relation":"opened-from","type":"view","viewId":"c6c0a107-7b3e-4d19-8a26-3e9d1c0b6a07"}],"requirements":["01a11544-5f68-7e07-a7e0-fa99257570f6"]},"variants":{"another-decisio